  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 108 PM MDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nFrom Friday through early next week, moisture will gradually be on \nthe increase. A weak disturbance moves across the region Friday late \nmorning and some guidance is printing out some light precip over the \nfar eastern plains. Although cant rule it out believe better chance \nof precip will be isolated precip in the afternoon /early evening \nplains and more scattered storms over the mtns, especially the San \nJuan region. Temps this day may be a degree or so warmer than \nThursdays max temps, especially over the plains.\n\nFor Saturday...A bit wetter this day, with guidance showing better \nchances for the plains, especially south and east of a line from \nKTAD to KLAA. Max temps similar to Fridays highs.\n\nSunday...RH fields throughout the column ramp up this day, and we \ncould see some heavier convection over the CONTDVD this day, with \nsome of the precip likely pushing out onto the plains. Sfc troughing \nis still noted over the far southeast plains, and once again the \nbest chance of showers may be over this region. With more clouds and \nprecip about, temps are expected to be 2-3F cooler than Saturdays \ntemps. \n\nInto next week, we should continue to see monsoonal showers and \nthunderstorms over the region as fairly stout mid level troughing is \nexpected to be over the Eastern PACific (EPAC), while the mid level \nridge remains over the central part of the country. This will keep \nmid level southwest flow ongoing and moisture will continue to be \ntapped from old Mexico and the subtropical EPAC. Actually, the \namount of precip next week may be dependent on how much mid/upper \nlevel moisture gets advected up from the Tropical Cyclones/tropical \ndisturbances that will  be in the EPAC/Mexico coast. Some guidance \nshows some fairly stout high RH values advecting northward, and this \ncould allow for the potential of numerous showers and t-storms over \nthe SW CONUS, including CO, during this period. \\/Hodanish",
